      "description": "The collaborative-development sub-graph — a NAMED SUB-GRAPH of this layer, OPT-IN: off in every layer, this one included, unless that layer lists `smart-base.collab` in its own `enableSubgraphs` (owner, 2026-11-13, check:optin-refs follow-up). It holds the processes that run on cat-harness's work plan and delivery process — they claim and close a bean, keep the work plan, or stage, preview and release a change: `smart-guideline-end-to-end`, `SGAuthoring.DAKLifecycle`, and DIIG's `diig-investment-path`. The L2 and L3 processes of the same kind are in each level's own opt-in collab group, `L2/collab/` and `L3/collab/` (`smart-base.L2-collab`, `smart-base.L3-collab`; owner, 2026-11-13: L2/L3 own collab). It `requires` `cat-harness.sdlc`, which requires `cat-harness.work-plan`, and the four knowledge-graph levels `smart-base-L1`..`smart-base-L4` whose skills its end-to-end process calls (owner, 2026-11-13), so switching it on switches all of them on. The graph inside it is declared FROM WITHIN, in `collab/graph.json`.",
